1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,498
Did the round design of the Parliament House come from this temple in Morena?

2
00:00:04,498 --> 00:00:08,246
On a lone hill stands a circular enclosure of stone.

3
00:00:08,246 --> 00:00:12,369
From the outside, it reminds you of the old Parliament in Delhi.

4
00:00:12,369 --> 00:00:15,742
But no written proof of this claim has been found.

5
00:00:15,742 --> 00:00:19,490
So what is the truth? Let's look at it with evidence.

6
00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:23,863
This temple has no roof in the middle.

7
00:00:23,863 --> 00:00:29,329
The courtyard is open straight to the sky. People say,

8
00:00:29,329 --> 00:00:32,608
it was left open on purpose.

9
00:00:32,608 --> 00:00:36,981
Because the 64 yoginis used to descend here from the sky.

10
00:00:36,981 --> 00:00:40,807
Yoginis are forms of the powers of the Goddess,

11
00:00:40,807 --> 00:00:43,540
who were believed to be able to fly.

12
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:47,183
But the stones have their own separate story.

13
00:00:47,183 --> 00:00:51,737
An inscription was found here, that is, writing carved on stone.

14
00:00:51,737 --> 00:00:56,747
It has a king's name, and a year written on it.

15
00:00:56,747 --> 00:00:59,479
In the middle there is a Shiva temple,

16
00:00:59,479 --> 00:01:02,211
and in the roof, stones with holes.

17
00:01:02,211 --> 00:01:06,310
These holes carried rainwater down.

18
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:09,348
In this video, we will go through the evidence one by one.

19
00:01:09,348 --> 00:01:11,247
First, what the scriptures say.

20
00:01:11,247 --> 00:01:13,906
Then, what the excavation and the report say.

21
00:01:13,906 --> 00:01:17,704
Then, where experts disagree. And finally,

22
00:01:17,704 --> 00:01:20,743
what you can see for yourself by going there.

23
00:01:20,743 --> 00:01:24,541
Each panel will say whether it is scripture, evidence,

24
00:01:24,541 --> 00:01:25,680
or just a story.

25
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,981
Let's start with the scriptures.

26
00:01:27,981 --> 00:01:31,203
The Agni Purana is an ancient Hindu scripture,

27
00:01:31,203 --> 00:01:33,964
which also has rules of worship.

28
00:01:33,964 --> 00:01:39,027
In its Tantra chapters, the names of the 64 yoginis are found.

29
00:01:39,027 --> 00:01:42,248
Tantra means a secret tradition of worship,

30
00:01:42,248 --> 00:01:45,930
in which mantras and mandalas are very important.

31
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:53,286
According to the Agni Purana, these yoginis stand around the Bhairava form of Shiva.

32
00:01:53,286 --> 00:01:57,424
Each one has her own name and her own invocation.

33
00:01:57,424 --> 00:02:01,103
Invocation means the way of calling them in worship.

34
00:02:01,103 --> 00:02:04,781
This forms a circle, with Shiva in the middle,

35
00:02:04,781 --> 00:02:06,620
and the powers all around.

36
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:11,086
The scripture also describes the arrangement of a round mandala.

37
00:02:11,086 --> 00:02:15,552
A mandala is a sacred circular diagram made for worship.

38
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:20,018
Now think, if this diagram were built in stone.

39
00:02:20,018 --> 00:02:23,144
What would it look like? A temple in the middle,

40
00:02:23,144 --> 00:02:26,270
and small rooms in a round wall.

41
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:30,388
Now comes the folk tale, which has no written proof.

42
00:02:30,388 --> 00:02:35,420
The village elders say the yoginis used to fly in at night.

43
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:38,623
That is why the courtyard was never given a roof.

44
00:02:38,623 --> 00:02:42,282
This story has been passed down from generation to generation.

45
00:02:42,282 --> 00:02:46,400
We will call it just a story, and we will respect it.

46
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,986
There is another story going around too. They say,

47
00:02:49,986 --> 00:02:53,123
this temple was a kind of school.

48
00:02:53,123 --> 00:02:58,054
Here, mathematics and astrology were taught by watching the movement of the sun.

49
00:02:58,054 --> 00:03:02,088
Jyotish, or astrology, means calculating the movements of the planets and stars.

50
00:03:02,088 --> 00:03:06,570
But this is also a folk tale, no inscription says this.

51
00:03:06,570 --> 00:03:11,666
So the texts give us 64 yoginis and a circular mandala.

52
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:16,761
The folk tale gives us flying yoginis and a school of the sun.

53
00:03:16,761 --> 00:03:21,347
But what do the stones say? When it was built, who built it,

54
00:03:21,347 --> 00:03:24,914
and who first told the world about it?

55
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:29,500
Now let's move toward the research, with proof.

56
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,951
This temple is in Morena district of Madhya Pradesh,

57
00:03:32,951 --> 00:03:37,170
near Mitaoli village. Some people also call it Mitawali.

58
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:40,238
For centuries it stood quietly on the hill.

59
00:03:40,238 --> 00:03:42,155
The villagers knew about it,

60
00:03:42,155 --> 00:03:45,990
but it was not on the maps of the outside world.

61
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:48,813
Then comes M. B. Garde,

62
00:03:48,813 --> 00:03:51,635
an officer of the Gwalior State Archaeological Department.

63
00:03:51,635 --> 00:03:54,928
He carried out a proper survey of this temple.

64
00:03:54,928 --> 00:03:59,633
A survey means measuring a place, examining it, and preparing a written report.

65
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:07,160
The first mention of this temple is found in his report from around 1915.

66
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:11,381
Garde did not just look at the temple, he also read its inscriptions.

67
00:04:11,381 --> 00:04:15,181
That was the real work of research in those days.

68
00:04:15,181 --> 00:04:19,824
Reading the letters carved on stone, writing them down, and preserving them.

69
00:04:19,824 --> 00:04:24,890
Because of this very report, later historians reached this temple.

70
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:29,316
Then, after independence, a big step was taken.

71
00:04:29,316 --> 00:04:35,402
The Archaeological Survey of India, that is ASI, is the country's archaeology organization.

72
00:04:35,402 --> 00:04:39,828
Archaeology means the science of old things and old places.

73
00:04:39,828 --> 00:04:47,020
ASI declared this circular temple a protected monument of national importance.

74
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:50,669
This declaration was made in 1951. It means

75
00:04:50,669 --> 00:04:55,881
this temple is now under the protection of law. Here, damage,

76
00:04:55,881 --> 00:04:59,530
encroachment or arbitrary construction is not allowed.

77
00:04:59,530 --> 00:05:05,264
That is, the government accepted that these stones belong not just to the village,

78
00:05:05,264 --> 00:05:07,870
but are the heritage of the whole country.

79
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:12,848
Now there is a report, and also the protection of law.

80
00:05:12,848 --> 00:05:18,932
But the real question is still left. What is inside the temple?

81
00:05:18,932 --> 00:05:22,803
How many rooms are there, what's in the middle,

82
00:05:22,803 --> 00:05:26,122
and what does that inscription say?

83
00:05:26,122 --> 00:05:29,440
Come, let's climb the hill and go inside.

84
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:33,066
As soon as you reach the top, you see a big round wall.

85
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:37,498
Inside this wall, small rooms are built all around.

86
00:05:37,498 --> 00:05:40,721
These rooms are called cells or chambers.

87
00:05:40,721 --> 00:05:44,750
In front of each room there is a small section with pillars.

88
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,570
The whole circle looks like a wheel.

89
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:52,794
Now listen to the count. This round wall has 65 rooms.

90
00:05:52,794 --> 00:05:58,541
Scholars guess that there was one room for each yogini.

91
00:05:58,541 --> 00:06:02,198
And one room for the Goddess herself.

92
00:06:02,198 --> 00:06:06,900
Today most of the rooms are empty, and the statues are not seen there.

93
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:11,136
In the open courtyard in the middle there is a round temple,

94
00:06:11,136 --> 00:06:13,490
which is dedicated to Shiva.

95
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:17,726
So the layout described in the texts can be seen here in stone.

96
00:06:17,726 --> 00:06:21,963
Shiva in the middle, and rooms of the shaktis all around.

97
00:06:21,963 --> 00:06:26,670
There is no roof over the courtyard, only open sky.

98
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:31,260
Scholars call such an open temple a hypaethral temple.

99
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:34,320
Hypaethral means one that has no roof,

100
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:37,380
one that is directly under the sky.

101
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:41,460
This feature is often seen in yogini temples.

102
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:45,030
Folk tales explain the reason as flying yoginis,

103
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:48,600
but the stone itself gives no reason.

104
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,692
Now look at the most interesting thing.

105
00:06:50,692 --> 00:06:54,875
On the roof of the middle temple there are stone slabs.

106
00:06:54,875 --> 00:06:57,803
These slabs have small holes in them.

107
00:06:57,803 --> 00:07:01,568
Rainwater used to go down through these holes.

108
00:07:01,568 --> 00:07:06,170
And it collected in a big tank under the ground.

109
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:10,097
In today's language, this is called rainwater harvesting.

110
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:15,770
That is, saving rainwater carefully instead of letting it flow away wasted.

111
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:20,133
On a dry hill, this was a very useful thing.

112
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:24,060
A temple for worship, and a water arrangement as well.

113
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:25,487
Now, that inscription.

114
00:07:25,487 --> 00:07:31,194
In the writing carved on one stone slab, the year 1323 is written.

115
00:07:31,194 --> 00:07:35,474
This year is according to the Christian era, that is, CE.

116
00:07:35,474 --> 00:07:40,230
The writing has the name of Devapala, king of the Kachchhapaghata dynasty.

117
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:44,510
That is, the temple work was done under the king's patronage.

118
00:07:44,510 --> 00:07:48,498
Who were the Kachchhapaghata? It was a medieval royal dynasty,

119
00:07:48,498 --> 00:07:51,600
which ruled in this area.

120
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:55,587
Medieval means the period between ancient and modern times.

121
00:07:55,587 --> 00:08:00,461
The name of the king of this same dynasty can still be read on this temple's stone.

122
00:08:00,461 --> 00:08:03,120
can still be read today.

123
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:07,531
So now we have both the name and the year.

124
00:08:07,531 --> 00:08:09,295
It seems the story is over.

125
00:08:09,295 --> 00:08:12,823
But this is where the real debate begins.

126
00:08:12,823 --> 00:08:16,793
Is this inscription the date the temple was built?

127
00:08:16,793 --> 00:08:19,880
Or the date of repairs to an older temple?

128
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:23,850
And the Parliament House question is still left.

129
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:27,900
First, the dispute over the date. Some historians say,

130
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:31,950
the 1323 inscription is the date the temple was built.

131
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:36,000
Others say the temple was built well before this.

132
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:40,050
And the Kachchhapaghata kings had it repaired later.

133
00:08:40,050 --> 00:08:44,100
There are scholars on both sides, and both have their own arguments.

134
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,672
The root of the dispute is just one thing.

135
00:08:46,672 --> 00:08:49,673
No foundation inscription was found here.

136
00:08:49,673 --> 00:08:55,245
A foundation inscription means the inscription that is placed at the time of construction.

137
00:08:55,245 --> 00:08:57,817
If there were one, the matter would be clear.

138
00:08:57,817 --> 00:09:01,247
An archaeology report also says the same,

139
00:09:01,247 --> 00:09:03,390
that is why there is disagreement over the date.

140
00:09:03,390 --> 00:09:06,165
Now the next, and the most famous, controversy.

141
00:09:06,165 --> 00:09:09,866
The old Parliament House in Delhi is also round.

142
00:09:09,866 --> 00:09:14,954
Outside, there is a long row of pillars all around. Looking from above,

143
00:09:14,954 --> 00:09:19,117
the shapes of the two look quite similar.

144
00:09:19,117 --> 00:09:23,280
That is why people say the design was taken from here.

145
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,135
One side says,

146
00:09:25,135 --> 00:09:29,308
British architects had seen India's temples.

147
00:09:29,308 --> 00:09:34,409
It could be that they took inspiration from this round temple.

148
00:09:34,409 --> 00:09:38,118
This claim goes around a lot on social media.

149
00:09:38,118 --> 00:09:41,828
But behind this claim, no written document,

150
00:09:41,828 --> 00:09:44,610
no letter or plan has been found.

151
00:09:44,610 --> 00:09:48,494
The other side says this could just be a coincidence.

152
00:09:48,494 --> 00:09:53,932
In those days, round buildings and pillars were common in Europe's neoclassical style.

153
00:09:53,932 --> 00:09:58,204
Neoclassical means a building style inspired by ancient Greece and Rome.

154
00:09:58,204 --> 00:10:01,700
So the round shape could have come from there too.

155
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:06,775
So what do we say? We say this claim is disputed.

156
00:10:06,775 --> 00:10:11,850
The similar shape is a fact, you can see it with your eyes.

157
00:10:11,850 --> 00:10:15,910
But proof of copying has not been found yet.

158
00:10:15,910 --> 00:10:20,985
Until documents are found, it is not right to call it proven.

159
00:10:20,985 --> 00:10:24,030
And calling it false would also be hasty.

160
00:10:24,030 --> 00:10:29,346
Now let's talk about the questions that nobody has an answer to.

161
00:10:29,346 --> 00:10:34,661
Like every old place, this one has some gaps too.

162
00:10:34,661 --> 00:10:36,594
Empty rooms, unfinished dates,

163
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:40,460
and a round wall standing silently.

164
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:43,360
Let's look at them one by one.

165
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:46,224
The first question: where did the statues go?

166
00:10:46,224 --> 00:10:50,997
The outer rooms must once have held statues of yoginis.

167
00:10:50,997 --> 00:10:56,248
They are not there today. When they were removed, and who removed them,

168
00:10:56,248 --> 00:10:58,634
is still not known.

169
00:10:58,634 --> 00:11:02,930
No record gives a direct answer to this question.

170
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:08,048
Next question: when was it actually built? An inscription gives a year,

171
00:11:08,048 --> 00:11:13,165
but whether it is for the construction or for repairs is not clear.

172
00:11:13,165 --> 00:11:17,353
If the temple was built earlier, then who built it first?

173
00:11:17,353 --> 00:11:21,540
This question is still open among historians today.

174
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,764
And there is this question too,

175
00:11:23,764 --> 00:11:26,877
why is this temple so round?

176
00:11:26,877 --> 00:11:29,991
Was it just a plan of a mandala?

177
00:11:29,991 --> 00:11:33,549
Or some way of tracking the movement of the sun?

178
00:11:33,549 --> 00:11:36,217
The scripture talks about the mandala.

179
00:11:36,217 --> 00:11:41,110
Folklore talks about the sun. The stones are still silent.

180
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:45,576
And the last question: what really happened here?

181
00:11:45,576 --> 00:11:50,042
Folklore says tantric rituals were performed here at night.

182
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:52,523
Another story says,

183
00:11:52,523 --> 00:11:55,997
mathematics and astrology were studied here.

184
00:11:55,997 --> 00:11:59,470
There is no written proof of either.

185
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:03,440
Maybe the truth lies somewhere between the two.

186
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:07,122
Now the best part. This temple still stands today,

187
00:12:07,122 --> 00:12:09,332
and you can go there.

188
00:12:09,332 --> 00:12:14,118
It is on a lonely hill near Mitaoli village in Morena district.

189
00:12:14,118 --> 00:12:16,328
The hill is about 30 metres high.

190
00:12:16,328 --> 00:12:20,010
The circular wall can be seen from far away.

191
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:24,084
To reach the temple you have to climb 100 steps.

192
00:12:24,084 --> 00:12:28,159
You will get a little tired, but the view from the top will make you forget everything.

193
00:12:28,159 --> 00:12:32,641
Open fields all around, and a round ring of stone in the middle.

194
00:12:32,641 --> 00:12:35,900
Go in the morning or evening, when the sun is gentle.

195
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:41,402
Once you are up there, do see these things. The empty rooms of the round wall,

196
00:12:41,402 --> 00:12:45,905
and the pillars in front of them. The Shiva temple in the middle,

197
00:12:45,905 --> 00:12:49,906
and its roof with an opening. And the open courtyard,

198
00:12:49,906 --> 00:12:52,908
from where you can see the sky directly.

199
00:12:52,908 --> 00:12:57,910
Standing here, you can feel the folklore.

200
00:12:57,910 --> 00:13:02,734
One thing to remember. This is an ASI protected monument.

201
00:13:02,734 --> 00:13:08,040
Writing on the walls, breaking stones, or littering is not allowed.

202
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:12,863
This heritage is ours, and our future generations' too.

203
00:13:12,863 --> 00:13:16,240
Leave it just as you found it.

204
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:19,812
So now all the evidence is in front of you.

205
00:13:19,812 --> 00:13:23,894
The texts describe a circular mandala of 64 yoginis.

206
00:13:23,894 --> 00:13:28,996
The stones give us an inscription from 1323 and a circular temple.

207
00:13:28,996 --> 00:13:35,119
But there is still no written proof of the claim about the Parliament House.

208
00:13:35,119 --> 00:13:36,650
The decision is yours.

209
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:39,556
Now, one simple question for you.

210
00:13:39,556 --> 00:13:45,367
Was the circular shape of the Parliament House inspired by this temple,

211
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:51,179
or is it just a coincidence? Just write in the comments: inspiration or coincidence.

212
00:13:51,179 --> 00:13:56,990
Next time we will go to another mysterious place,

213
00:13:56,990 --> 00:13:58,733
with proof.
